(12. Reporting and accountable decisions) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.1 The graph is not the final deliverable) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The purpose of an assessment is not to produce an impressive network visualization. The) Tj
T*
(graph is an analytical substrate. The report must translate graph context into claims,) Tj
T*
(evidence, findings and decisions without hiding scope or uncertainty.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The canonical Reporting Standard requires an assessment identity, versioned scope, method) Tj
T*
(and limitations, estate and AIBOM view, trust and boundary view, authority view, control) Tj
T*
(assessment, path portfolio, maturity profile, scorecards and coverage, findings, decisions,) Tj
T*
(roadmap, limitations and sign-off [ATG-9]. Executive reporting must disclose critical gates,) Tj
T*
(coverage and residual uncertainty rather than reduce the result to a traffic light.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.2 Findings remain separate from disposition) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A finding records the technical or assurance condition. Management acceptance, exception or) Tj
T*
(treatment records what the organization decides to do about it. Acceptance does not make the) Tj
T*
(underlying condition disappear. This separation preserves technical integrity and allows) Tj
T*
(future reviewers to understand whether risk changed or only its disposition changed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.3 Traceability survives to the decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A defensible decision should be traceable back to the evidence and graph context that) Tj
T*
(support it. This is particularly important for consequential AI because policy statements) Tj
T*
(and high-level risk language can otherwise become disconnected from the actual system path.) Tj
T*
(ATG's reporting discipline is intended to preserve the chain from observed state to) Tj
T*
(accountable action.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(13. Limitations and current validation status) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(13.1 Methodological coherence is not empirical validation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A governed methodology can be internally coherent without having demonstrated that) Tj
T*
(independent assessors will apply it consistently across real organizations. The current) Tj
T*
(artifact stack includes synthetic calibration material and a reproducibility protocol, but) Tj
T*
(the frozen baseline explicitly records inter-assessor reproducibility validation as a) Tj
T*
(pending external gate.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(13.2 Synthetic cases are not field proof) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Artifact #10 contains synthetic reference cases designed for calibration, adversarial checks) Tj
T*
(and reasoning consistency. They must not be represented as observed facts about real vendors) Tj
T*
(or organizations. A synthetic worked example can demonstrate how rules interact; it cannot) Tj
T*
(prove predictive validity, business impact or external effectiveness.) Tj
T*
() Tj
